WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.296
Module seven. Orders and dispatch.

2
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:10.215
This is where everything comes together: a customer orders, and the vendor delivers.

3
00:00:10.665 --> 00:00:12.627
We'll look at the order management page.

4
00:00:13.077 --> 00:00:16.235
How to verify and accept an order, item by item.

5
00:00:16.685 --> 00:00:18.967
What happens with multi vendor orders.

6
00:00:19.417 --> 00:00:22.297
Dispatch through Shiprocket, with its three services.

7
00:00:22.747 --> 00:00:24.731
And local drivers, as a backup.

8
00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:31.122
In the vendor console, open Orders. At the top are four numbers.

9
00:00:31.572 --> 00:00:35.796
Awaiting action: new orders that need to be verified and accepted.

10
00:00:35.796 --> 00:00:36.948
Keep this at zero.

11
00:00:37.398 --> 00:00:40.577
In fulfilment: accepted orders being picked and packed.

12
00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:43.672
On the road: orders dispatched to the customer.

13
00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:47.664
And open value: the total value of all open orders.

14
00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:51.838
Every order follows this path.

15
00:00:52.288 --> 00:00:54.677
A new order arrives in the vendor console.

16
00:00:55.127 --> 00:00:58.690
The vendor verifies each item against their stock, and accepts.

17
00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:04.161
The team picks and packs the order. The status keeps updating in the admin panel and

18
00:01:04.161 --> 00:01:05.177
The customer app.

19
00:01:05.627 --> 00:01:07.120
The vendor clicks handover.

20
00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:11.154
And the order is dispatched, through Shiprocket or a local driver.

21
00:01:13.567 --> 00:01:17.940
Some customer orders have many items. Here's how Oribrix handles that.

22
00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:22.038
A vendor can accept only the items they can actually supply.

23
00:01:22.488 --> 00:01:26.051
The items they don't select start looking for another nearby vendor.

24
00:01:26.501 --> 00:01:29.338
When another vendor accepts them, the order is split.

25
00:01:29.788 --> 00:01:32.805
And the customer app shows two separate shipments.

26
00:01:32.805 --> 00:01:36.124
This is normal, so explain it to customers if they ask.

27
00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:40.453
Let's watch this in the live demo.

28
00:01:45.067 --> 00:01:49.590
We start in the vendor's inventory, and a new order has come in, from Bengaluru.

29
00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:21.837
The order opens with a products verification list.

30
00:02:21.837 --> 00:02:25.387
Each item shows the quantity, price and available stock.

31
00:02:41.067 --> 00:02:45.447
The vendor ticks the items they can supply. Select all ticks everything.

32
00:02:45.447 --> 00:02:47.638
The delivery address is shown below.

33
00:02:58.667 --> 00:03:04.061
Verify and accept. Any item not ticked goes to another vendor, and the customer sees

34
00:03:04.061 --> 00:03:04.960
Two shipments.

35
00:03:13.867 --> 00:03:17.169
After handover, the vendor can dispatch through Shiprocket.

36
00:03:17.169 --> 00:03:19.072
Here's what happens automatically.

37
00:03:19.522 --> 00:03:24.851
Shiprocket picks the best available courier partner, like Delhivery, BlueDart or

38
00:03:24.851 --> 00:03:25.517
Shadowfax.

39
00:03:25.967 --> 00:03:29.359
It assigns an AWB, which is the tracking number.

40
00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.580
It generates the shipping label.

41
00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:34.568
And it schedules pickup from the vendor's warehouse.

42
00:03:36.967 --> 00:03:38.887
Let's watch this in the live demo.

43
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:47.439
This is order management. You can see the four numbers, and the order list with

44
00:03:47.439 --> 00:03:50.679
Customer, warehouse, items, amount, payment and stage.

45
00:04:10.700 --> 00:04:15.963
The dispatch order window has two tabs: Shiprocket courier, which is automatic, and

46
00:04:15.963 --> 00:04:17.548
Local or in-house driver.

47
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.994
It shows the destination, and the pickup warehouse.

48
00:04:32.994 --> 00:04:35.724
Dispatch via Shiprocket creates the shipment.

49
00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:54.423
One important point from the session: the vendor's warehouse must already be

50
00:04:54.423 --> 00:04:56.684
Verified inside the Shiprocket portal.

51
00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.715
This is an admin job, and it can't be done from the Oribrix admin panel.

52
00:05:16.715 --> 00:05:21.621
Before approving a vendor's warehouse, open the Shiprocket portal and verify the

53
00:05:21.621 --> 00:05:25.055
Pickup address there. Shiprocket tracks by phone number.

54
00:05:25.055 --> 00:05:29.776
A new vendor's phone number needs an OTP once, so coordinate with the vendor.

55
00:05:29.776 --> 00:05:34.743
If the same vendor adds another warehouse with the same number, no OTP is needed.

56
00:05:34.743 --> 00:05:37.687
This becomes part of the vendor's KYC lifecycle.

57
00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:37.328
Shiprocket has three services. This is where unit weight from module four matters.

58
00:06:37.778 --> 00:06:41.563
Normal delivery, for orders under five hundred kilos.

59
00:06:41.563 --> 00:06:42.706
Its API is live.

60
00:06:43.156 --> 00:06:47.463
Shiprocket cargo, for bulk orders over five hundred kilos.

61
00:06:47.463 --> 00:06:49.023
Its API is also live.

62
00:06:49.473 --> 00:06:54.987
And express. There's no express API yet, so express orders currently go as normal

63
00:06:54.987 --> 00:06:57.302
Delivery, or are created manually.

64
00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:03.241
Until the express API arrives, here's the manual process.

65
00:07:03.691 --> 00:07:06.571
A customer places an order with express delivery.

66
00:07:07.021 --> 00:07:08.856
Copy the Oribrix order ID.

67
00:07:09.306 --> 00:07:10.906
Open the Shiprocket portal.

68
00:07:11.356 --> 00:07:13.959
Create the order there manually, as express.

69
00:07:14.409 --> 00:07:16.115
And keep the customer updated.

70
00:07:18.500 --> 00:07:20.420
Let's watch this in the live demo.

71
00:07:24.233 --> 00:07:29.564
Now the second tab: local or in-house driver. This is for when Shiprocket cancels,

72
00:07:29.564 --> 00:07:31.124
Or can't take the order.

73
00:07:52.233 --> 00:07:56.876
Quick select picks a saved delivery partner, or you can type a new one: name and

74
00:07:56.876 --> 00:07:57.630
Phone number.

75
00:08:12.233 --> 00:08:16.317
The customer receives this phone number, to call the driver for delivery

76
00:08:16.317 --> 00:08:17.054
Coordination.

77
00:08:32.233 --> 00:08:37.006
Then the vehicle model, like Tata Ace, and the vehicle number, which is optional.

78
00:08:37.006 --> 00:08:38.420
Dispatch and link phone.

79
00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:56.841
To use local drivers well, set them up in advance.

80
00:08:57.291 --> 00:09:00.811
The delivery partner's name, or quick select a saved driver.

81
00:09:01.261 --> 00:09:05.293
A phone number. The customer will call this number, so it must be correct.

82
00:09:05.743 --> 00:09:06.874
The vehicle model.

83
00:09:07.324 --> 00:09:10.246
The vehicle number. It's optional, but recommended.

84
00:09:10.696 --> 00:09:14.686
Vendors should add their drivers in the Drivers and Fleet section first.

85
00:09:15.136 --> 00:09:18.016
There, each driver shows as on trip, or idle.

86
00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:25.705
Know this limitation. When a local driver is used, the customer does not get the

87
00:09:25.705 --> 00:09:31.209
Shiprocket tracking SMS. The app shows the source and destination, but support must

88
00:09:31.209 --> 00:09:36.315
Keep the customer updated. So use local drivers as a backup, not the default.

89
00:10:12.133 --> 00:10:14.053
Let's watch this in the live demo.

90
00:10:18.667 --> 00:10:22.294
Back in the dispatch window. The Shiprocket tab is the default.

91
00:10:49.067 --> 00:10:53.854
In the order details, you see the products with their status, the delivery address,

92
00:10:53.854 --> 00:10:58.006
And two buttons: Cancel order, and Handover and assign delivery partner.

93
00:11:10.667 --> 00:11:14.422
Once dispatched, the order shows on trip, and moves to on the road.

94
00:11:23.467 --> 00:11:26.198
Here's a dispatch checklist for vendors and support.

95
00:11:26.648 --> 00:11:29.122
Accept only items you truly have in stock.

96
00:11:29.572 --> 00:11:31.130
Pack, then click handover.

97
00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:34.225
Make sure the warehouse is verified in Shiprocket.

98
00:11:34.675 --> 00:11:38.003
Heavy orders over five hundred kilos go by cargo.

99
00:11:38.453 --> 00:11:41.141
Express orders are created manually for now.

100
00:11:41.591 --> 00:11:45.818
And with a local driver, use the correct phone number, and keep the customer

101
00:11:45.818 --> 00:11:46.263
Updated.

102
00:11:48.667 --> 00:11:52.486
Quick check. Shiprocket cancelled a pickup. What's the backup option?

103
00:11:56.436 --> 00:12:01.624
Dispatch with a local or in-house driver, from the second tab in the dispatch

104
00:12:01.624 --> 00:12:07.217
Window. And remember, support must update the customer, because there's no tracking

105
00:12:07.217 --> 00:12:07.486
SMS.

106
00:12:10.300 --> 00:12:11.879
Let's sum up module seven.

107
00:12:12.329 --> 00:12:17.598
Verify and accept item by item. Anything not accepted goes to another vendor.

108
00:12:18.048 --> 00:12:19.733
Pack, handover, then dispatch.

109
00:12:20.183 --> 00:12:22.871
Every warehouse must be verified in Shiprocket.

110
00:12:23.321 --> 00:12:28.377
Normal under five hundred kilos, cargo above, and express is manual for now.

111
00:12:28.827 --> 00:12:32.576
And local drivers are a backup only, with no tracking SMS.

112
00:12:32.576 --> 00:12:37.489
In the last module, we'll cover payouts, disputes, and what's still pending.

113
00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:45.489
That's the end of module 7. Next up, module 8: Payouts, disputes and what's pending.
